id: query-options
title: Query Options
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the best ways to share "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" between multiple places, yet keep them co-located to one another, is to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it, but it has a lot of advantages when using it "},{"type":"link","href":"../typescript.md#typing-query-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"with TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can define all possible options for a query in one place, and you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { queryOptions, noop } from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root',\n})\nexport class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  post(postId: number) {\n    return queryOptions({\n      queryKey: ['post', postId],\n      queryFn: () => {\n        return lastValueFrom(\n          this.http.get<Post>(\n            `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${postId}`,\n          ),\n        )\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// usage:\n\npostId = input.required({\n  transform: numberAttribute,\n})\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\npostQuery = injectQuery(() => this.queries.post(this.postId()))\n\nqueryClient.query(this.queries.post(23)).catch(noop)\nqueryClient.setQueryData(this.queries.post(42).queryKey, newPost)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Infinite Queries, a separate "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"infiniteQueryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" helper is available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can still override some options at the component level. A very common and useful pattern is to create per-component "},{"type":"link","href":"./render-optimizations.md#select","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"}]},{"type":"text","value":" functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Type inference still works, so groupQuery.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\ngroupQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.title,\n}))","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nOne of the best ways to share `queryKey` and `queryFn` between multiple places, yet keep them co-located to one another, is to use the `queryOptions` helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it, but it has a lot of advantages when using it [with TypeScript](../typescript.md#typing-query-options). You can define all possible options for a query in one place, and you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them.\n\n\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions, noop } from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root',\n})\nexport class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  post(postId: number) {\n    return queryOptions({\n      queryKey: ['post', postId],\n      queryFn: () => {\n        return lastValueFrom(\n          this.http.get<Post>(\n            `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${postId}`,\n          ),\n        )\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// usage:\n\npostId = input.required({\n  transform: numberAttribute,\n})\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\npostQuery = injectQuery(() => this.queries.post(this.postId()))\n\nqueryClient.query(this.queries.post(23)).catch(noop)\nqueryClient.setQueryData(this.queries.post(42).queryKey, newPost)\n```\n\n\n\nFor Infinite Queries, a separate [`infiniteQueryOptions`](../reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md) helper is available.\n\n\n\nYou can still override some options at the component level. A very common and useful pattern is to create per-component [`select`](./render-optimizations.md#select) functions:\n\n\n\n\n```ts\n// Type inference still works, so groupQuery.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\ngroupQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.title,\n}))\n```\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-options\ntitle: Query Options\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/query-options.md\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions, noop } from '@tanstack/angular-query-experimental'\n\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root',\n})\nexport class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  post(postId: number) {\n    return queryOptions({\n      queryKey: ['post', postId],\n      queryFn: () => {\n        return lastValueFrom(\n          this.http.get<Post>(\n            `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${postId}`,\n          ),\n        )\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// usage:\n\npostId = input.required({\n  transform: numberAttribute,\n})\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\npostQuery = injectQuery(() => this.queries.post(this.postId()))\n\nqueryClient.query(this.queries.post(23)).catch(noop)\nqueryClient.setQueryData(this.queries.post(42).queryKey, newPost)\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```ts\n// Type inference still works, so groupQuery.data will be the return type of select instead of queryFn\nqueries = inject(QueriesService)\n\ngroupQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n  ...groupOptions(1),\n  select: (data) => data.title,\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n"}
